<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#fromUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The direction of action, IEC 60050-351, 351-44-05, is carried by this relation together with toUnit rather than by a class of its own.\r\n\r\nNote 2 of that entry states that the direction of action need not agree with the direction of the mass or energy flow. Modelling it as a class would invite an alignment to equate it with the direction of a flow in the technical process pattern, where a flow does transport material."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasFeedbackPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlLoop> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisesFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a physical unit to a functional unit it realises."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#PassiveFault> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-56-23."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alarm"@en .
_:N6af14bebfb584f6785f48335c5e61a25 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:Nc9d22fde771e4dd097059107d4ab0e20 .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named characteristic of the behaviour of a system or a transfer element, such as a settling time or an overshoot, to which a model assigns a value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ClosedAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An action in a closed action path in which the output variable is continuously or sequentially influencing the input variable and thus continuously or sequentially influencing itself."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#InputVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#VariableQuantity> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ReferenceVariableGeneratingElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-49-10. The German term is Fuehrungsgroessenbildner. Its note states that such an element often ensures that critical limits are not exceeded, for example by limiting the rate of change."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisesFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The inverse of realisedByPhysicalUnit, so that a model can start from a device.\r\n\r\nNote that the answer may name several units. IEC 60050-351 keeps the functional and the physical view apart on purpose, 351-56-02 against 351-56-03, and one device may realise a comparing element and a controlling element at once. A question asking what role a device plays therefore has more than one answer where the device carries more than one function, and that is the correct result rather than an ambiguity to remove."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Stability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlDifferenceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
