<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControlledVariableGeneration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Not a term of the standard.** IEC 60050-351 draws this unit at the right-hand edge of Figures 1 and 2, where x enters and q leaves the control system, but gives it no entry, no number and no index line. A search of the full text finds the wording only inside the two figures.\r\n\r\nThe class is nevertheless kept, because the final controlled variable it produces is a term of the standard, 351-48-10, and without a unit for it that variable would have no origin in a model. The last step of both figures would then go unrecorded.\r\n\r\nAnyone aligning this pattern with another should treat the class as a construct of this work rather than as normative vocabulary. REFERENCE.md lists it under the elements taken from the figures instead of from the entries."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControllingEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A functional unit consisting of the actuator and the final controlling element."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Signal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A physical variable quantity, one or more parameters of which carry information about one or more variable quantities."@en .
