<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControlledVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-48-10, marked q in Figures 1 and 2.\r\n\r\nThe entry adds that the final controlled variable need not belong to the control loop itself: where a mixture composition cannot be measured directly, a dependent property such as density or thermal conductivity is used as the controlled variable while the composition remains the final controlled variable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasFeedbackPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FeedbackPath> .
