<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#carriesInformationParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a signal to a parameter of it that represents information."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasCharacteristicValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has characteristic value"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#DegreeOfAutomation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-42-31. May be given only for a defined system whose limits are specified. Full automatic operation means all functions except switching on and off are automated."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ForwardPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An action path connecting the output of a comparing element to the output of the controlled system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#CharacteristicValue> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ManipulatedVariable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Alarm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "To indicate that the system has switched or will immediately switch to a state which is outside the specified operating conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Notify> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-43-05. Directed outside the system, as against alerting, 351-43-06, which is directed inside it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:N6af14bebfb584f6785f48335c5e61a25 .
_:Na9d0e8edea98435bb928b38298a2bd4a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Optimize> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "To design a process or act upon a process such that the performance criterion used for evaluating the process states assumes a value either as large or as small as possible within given limitations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#performsFunction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-43. Mapping an application onto the tasks the standard names keeps a model connected to existing plant documentation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Observer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-31. Structurally the definition of what practice calls a soft sensor, without the standard assuming any particular technique."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#runsOverActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionPath> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#RobustControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Closed-loop control able to keep system properties within a prescribed area even if the properties of the controlled system or of the controller deviate from those assumed for the design."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalSafety> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Functional Safety"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Redundancy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#SensingElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-56-26, with a thermocouple, a foil strain gauge and a pH electrode as its examples. The standard defines no term sensor; this is the entry practice means by it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#usesModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasManipulatedVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActiveFault> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#System> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#carriesInformationParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#InformationParameter> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasFeedbackPath> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-08."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#SamplingControl> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Monitor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-43-03. One of the tasks data driven applications typically occupy."@en .
_:N2284858a1e474ac8a4a84b7bf9a1b95a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Notify> .
