<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#partOfActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionLine> .
_:N2284858a1e474ac8a4a84b7bf9a1b95a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OpenAction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An action in an open action path, or in a closed action path where the output variable influences the input variable only under certain non-permanently acting conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ComputerControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Computer Control"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#MultivariableControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Multivariable Control"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FeedbackVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#VariableQuantity> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Control> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Fault> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fault"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisedByPhysicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-56-02 and 351-56-03 define the two as views of one item under consideration, taken by function and by construction.\r\n\r\nThe relation is the axis the technical process pattern lacks, where a technical resource is atomic. One physical unit may realise several functional units and one functional unit may be spread over several physical units, so no cardinality is asserted."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Actuator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A functional unit that generates the manipulated variable, required to drive the final controlling element, from the output variable of the controlling element."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ProgrammedControl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-20. The standard states no genus beyond control, so the class sits under Control. Storage-programmable logic control, 351-47-22, is a kind of this, which is how the standard covers what practice calls a programmable logic controller."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlledVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-48-01. Only a closed-loop control has one: it is what is measured and compared with the reference variable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlLoop> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
