_:N26e42a078c0846068152d5c44cb5811c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#partOfActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an action line to the action path it forms part of."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasControlledVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a closed-loop control to the controlled variable it acts upon."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasForwardPath> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Control> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Control"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#unit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasCharacteristicValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an item, a system or a control to a value it states for one of its characteristics."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ClosedActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An action path between the input variable and the output variable at which an additional action path goes back from the output variable to the input variable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ModelBasedControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ClosedLoopControl> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControllerOutputVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OutputVariable> .
_:N02471d87390f4cf483223b5cf166bb26 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "An ontology design pattern for the terminology of control technology, following DIN IEC 60050-351:2014, the International Electrotechnical Vocabulary. It models a control as a chain of action paths and actions, which is what allows open-loop and closed-loop control to be told apart by structure rather than by name: a closed-loop control requires a closed action, not merely a closed path. Around that it holds the variable quantities of a control loop, the items under consideration with their functional and physical units, the normative taxonomy of control functions, and the characteristics a device carries with their values and units. Seventy-nine classes drawn from 86 of the standard's 409 entries, with the selection documented entry by entry."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:Nd4cbbcd651df4c72b9c09b228a66d5c5 .
_:N17943a220dd949619c4dd934a1098a1e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#System> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Action> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Action"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#RealTimeCapability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlledVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The output variable of the controlled system that will be acted upon by one or more manipulated variables."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OutputVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#VariableQuantity> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControllingElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Controlling Element"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Control Equipment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an item or a system to a property it has, such as stability, observability or real-time capability."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#toUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an action line to the functional unit at which it ends."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Controllability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The property of a system implying that its state variables may be changed from an initial state into a desired final state within a finite time interval, via proper time variations of the input variables."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Fault> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fault in control equipment, classified by its effect on the output variables."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#fromUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an action line to the functional unit at which it starts."@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Monitor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlFunction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ProgrammedControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Programmed Control"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#PhysicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Physical Unit"@en .
