<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OpenLoopControl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-02. Characteristic for open-loop control is the open action path, or in a closed action path the fact that the output variables being influenced by the input variables are not continuously or sequentially influencing themselves and not by the same input variables.\r\n\r\nDeliberately **not** disjoint with closed-loop control: the standard admits open-loop control in a closed action path, so a disjointness axiom would contradict it. What separates the two is the action, not the path."@en .
