<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControlledVariableGeneration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControlledVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The variable quantity that the control is ultimately intended to influence, formed from the controlled variable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#isSourceOfActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The inverse of fromUnit. Together with the next one it says where a unit sits in the chain, and therefore whether it lies in the forward or in the feedback branch."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#DegreeOfAutomation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Action> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ItemUnderConsideration> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Action Path"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#AdaptiveControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adaptive Control"@en .
_:N67b8b06019cb4858b82554a0ba492620 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:Na0a1126dfd214f14836b04f756bc5b1d .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Warn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#symbol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
_:N11a08a0bafe54e3d93786c0f215cf32c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlDifferenceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The difference between the reference variable and the feedback variable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OpenAction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-06. The note to the entry states that a reset circuit, 351-47-62, has an open action although its structure has a closed action path.\r\n\r\nThis is the case that separates the pattern from the simplified reading that feedback alone makes a closed-loop control."@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#partOfControlledSystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Signal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#VariableQuantity> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Control> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-42-19. The German term is Leiten, which covers both open-loop and closed-loop control as well as the supervisory tasks around them. National footnote N1 of that entry states this explicitly: control is the general term here, and the narrower Regeln and Steuern belong to the entries below.\r\n\r\nNo class for automating sits between this class and the two kinds of control. The standard defines automating in 351-43 as a task, alongside measuring and monitoring, not in 351-47 as a kind of control, and 351-42-31 treats the degree of automation as a proportion of the functions of a system. A hand-operated closed-loop control is a closed-loop control by 351-47-01 without being automated, so a subclass axiom would state more than the standard does. Whether a control runs by itself is recorded through the AI pattern, where automation is a function, and the two are related in the alignment."@en .
_:N7a978177020247699c1b29ec0422a96f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ForwardPath> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ForwardPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionPath> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasControlledVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has controlled variable"@en .
_:Ne0b8edc2a98a4596b926cd45bc58c6bd <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlDifferenceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Control Difference Variable"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControllingElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A functional unit forming part of the controlled system and arranged at its input, driven by the manipulated variable and manipulating the mass flow or energy flow."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#PhysicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-56-03. The building view: the device as it is bought and installed. Not disjoint with the functional unit, since the two are views rather than kinds."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Optimize> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-43-14."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlDifferenceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#VariableQuantity> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Control> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Purposeful action on or in a process to meet specified objectives."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#TimeCharacteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Grouping of this pattern, so that a model may ask for the time behaviour without listing every characteristic by name."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Evaluate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlFunction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "Automation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#symbol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Characteristic> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#usesModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:Nf93a732929554f6890019aec78c78c29 .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A directed path within a control structure, which connects two selected variable quantities."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#carriesVariable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControllingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-49-02."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#symbol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
_:N0a6c6d946f364af9bd1e5360038e772f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-44-03 and 351-44-04. An action path is composed of action lines, which is what makes the path traceable through the units."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#partOfActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "part of action path"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ComputerControl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-52. No genus beyond control is stated."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#isSourceOfActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a functional unit to an action line starting at it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Monitor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "To acquire a quantity value continuously or sequentially in order to check whether it is within normal operating limits and, where appropriate, to signal if it passes its tolerance boundaries."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasDisturbanceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:N9217ccc9857e4c39831cc4c66960100e .
_:N4876783d5b2e4296bb5ba5f66c53abed <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDifferent> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#carriesInformationParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "carries information parameter"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OpenLoopControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A process whereby one or more variable quantities as input variables influence other variable quantities as output variables in accordance with the proper laws of the system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#partOfControlledSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlledSystem> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#InformationParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-41-18."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#isTargetOfActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is target of action line"@en .
