_:Nce7a80a29f9b4db4bf7f47974131a916 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Notify> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "To inform selected non-system clients about the occurrence of a specified event by a predefined message or indication."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#StateVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An element of the state vector of a system, from which together with the input variables the output variables are determined."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ReferenceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-48-02."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an action path to a part of it running between two functional units."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Intervene> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-43-15. The entry gives a normative form of what practice calls keeping a human in the loop, including the priority between units."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "IEC 60050-351"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasForwardPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a control loop to its forward path."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#QualityCharacteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Characteristic> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OpenActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Open Action Path"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#quantity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "quantity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Optimize> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Optimize"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#symbol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "symbol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControllingEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-49-09. The German term is Stelleinrichtung, drawn as the dashed grouping in Figures 1 and 2.\r\n\r\nIt groups the signal side, 351-49-07, and the element acting on the flow, 351-49-08, which the standard otherwise keeps apart. Membership is recorded through consistsOfUnit rather than through a subclass axiom, since the two parts stay units in their own right."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Intervene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intervene"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an automation to the arrangement of elements carrying it out, that is a control loop or a control chain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FinalControlledVariableGeneration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generation of the Final Controlled Variable"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#QualityCharacteristic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:N289829103cba4d99b56e838b0a627765 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#CascadeControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Closed-loop control in which the output variable of one controller is the reference variable of one or more secondary control loops."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#SensingElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A functional unit that senses the effect of a measurand at its input and places a corresponding measurement signal at its output."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#isTargetOfActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ReferenceVariable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#MeasuringElement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-49-05, where the full term is measuring element in control technology.\r\n\r\nNot the same entry as the sensing element, 351-56-26. The sensing element responds to the measurand, whereas this element produces the feedback variable that closes the action path. A model may realise both through one physical unit."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ModelBasedControl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-33. The definition names a real-time model of the process, which is the natural place for a data driven process model in a control structure."@en .
_:N899eabd481874d0ba1908f3194565ad7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Operate> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050/1.0.0> .
