<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-44-04, drawn as the arrows of Figures 1 and 2.\r\n\r\nThe class resolves an action path into the units it runs through. Without it a path can only be asserted to be open or closed; with it the assertion becomes checkable against the units and the variables actually recorded.\r\n\r\nDisjoint from the action path: a line is a part of a path, not a path of its own."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-56-24. A note to the entry includes the process control station and the operating manuals, which is how the standard covers what practice calls a control room."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Controller> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-49-11, where the full term is controller for closed-loop control."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "acts on"@en .
