_:Nb99c6fa9987a4e32a0d8c8e23b2505b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N17943a220dd949619c4dd934a1098a1e .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Controller> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "Helmut-Schmidt-Universität / Universität der Bundeswehr Hamburg" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#forCharacteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Functional: one value quantifies exactly one characteristic."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FeedbackVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A variable quantity which represents the controlled variable and is returned to the comparing element."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#toUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-44-05. Together with fromUnit it carries the direction of action."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#MeasuringElement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Normative basis: DIN IEC 60050-351:2014, identical to IEC 60050-351:2013.\r\n\r\nThe standard holds 409 entries and this pattern takes up 86 of them. REFERENCE.md lists every entry with the reason it is taken or left out, so the selection is checkable rather than asserted. Roughly 150 entries are the mathematical apparatus of control theory, such as transfer functions and Nyquist plots, which an engineering model names but never instantiates.\r\n\r\nThree readings of the standard are easy to get wrong and are therefore stated here. An actuator, 351-49-07, is the signal side driving the final controlling element, not the element acting on the flow. The final controlling element, 351-49-08, belongs to the controlled system, which this pattern records as a relation so that another pattern may hold it as a resource without contradiction. And the standard defines no sensor: it says sensing element, 351-56-26, and grades further by accuracy and signal standardisation.\r\n\r\nTerms the standard does not define, and which have to come from elsewhere: availability and reliability from IEC 60050-192, accuracy and resolution from IEC 60050-300, safety integrity from IEC 61508, and everything concerning data quality from ISO/IEC 22989."@en .
_:N22097a77f1e9426cb7733c9b2acd12c8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Alarm> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ProgrammableController> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Controller> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#MeasuringTransmitter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#PassiveFault> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#consistsOfUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisesFunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
_:N7dee3e4198ec4344bf528cafa0520978 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
