<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ControllingElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A functional unit that forms its output variable from the command variable in open-loop control and from the control difference variable in closed-loop control."@en .
_:N4876783d5b2e4296bb5ba5f66c53abed <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#distinctMembers> _:N22097a77f1e9426cb7733c9b2acd12c8 .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ClosedActionPath> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OpenActionPath> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#RuleBasedControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Closed-loop control in which the control algorithm explicitly incorporates one or more sets of rules."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:Nf3db27d227574c568187f6e629835c5d .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#consistsOfUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351 composes several units from others: the final controlling equipment from actuator and final controlling element, 351-49-09, the controller from comparing and controlling element, 351-49-11, and the control system from controlling and controlled system, 351-49-06.\r\n\r\nStated as a relation rather than through subclass axioms, since the parts remain units in their own right and one part may belong to more than one whole."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#isSourceOfActionLine> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#fromUnit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Action> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Control> .
_:Nc9d22fde771e4dd097059107d4ab0e20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Control> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ItemUnderConsideration> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#OptimalControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A type of control for which the performance index reaches a largest or smallest value under specified conditions."@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-11 and 351-47-12. A closed-loop control is carried by a loop, an open-loop control by a chain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#PhysicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An item under consideration defined according to construction or configuration."@en .
