<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#AdaptiveControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Closed-loop control with automatic modification of the structure or parameters of the controlling system to compensate for varying operating conditions and states."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#actionOverPath> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ActionPath> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "Control Technology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#FunctionalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Actuator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-49-07.\r\n\r\nThe German term is Steller, and the entry is the signal side of the manipulating equipment, not the element acting on the flow. That element is the final controlling element, 351-49-08. The common rendering of the German Aktor as actuator conflates the two and would put the wrong class on a valve."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#usesModel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-47-31 and 351-47-33. Both name a model of the controlled system as part of their structure."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#ModelBasedControl> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#usesModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a control or an observer to a model of the process it uses."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Plant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#realisedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "realised by"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Collects 351-42-20, -22, -23, -28, -31 and 351-54-06, which the standard states as properties of a system."@en .
_:Nd1b7b5ff370a4f9585780b52e889a2b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N39c6550557184428a5cff024b6188ecb .
