<http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#Fault> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Collecting class of this pattern for 351-56-22 and 351-56-23, which the standard states individually."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#hasVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has variable"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#RealTimeCapability> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "IEC 60050-351, 351-54-06, where the entry is stated for a process computer system.\r\n\r\nReal time is a capability of a system with a stated interval, not a property of time itself. The pattern follows that reading, so a model states the capability and the interval separately rather than calling a duration real time."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#SequentialControl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sequential Control"@en .
